{"body": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html><body style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.55;\">\n<div style=\"max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:32px 24px;\">\n\n<!-- COVER -->\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;\">FIELD MANUAL \u00b7 N\u00b0 01</div>\n<h1 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:42px;line-height:1.05;color:#1a1a1a;margin:8px 0 12px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Agentic Engineering<br><em style=\"color:#a08040;\">From scattered to system.</em></h1>\n<p style=\"color:#666666;font-style:italic;font-size:15px;margin:0 0 24px 0;\">Reverse-engineered from IndyDevDan's Tactical Agentic Coding curriculum \u2014 personalized to the TEST_AGENTS repo. Replaces $599 of info-product content.</p>\n<hr style=\"border:none;border-top:1px solid #cccccc;margin:24px 0;\">\n\n<!-- META -->\n<table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;width:100%;margin-bottom:24px;\">\n<tr><td style=\"color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.15em;font-weight:bold;width:130px;\">PREPARED FOR</td><td>Azeez Saba \u00b7 Dux Machina</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.15em;font-weight:bold;\">COMPILED</td><td>2026-05-11</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.15em;font-weight:bold;\">STATUS</td><td>Conceptual sweep complete \u00b7 Implementation pending</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 \u00a7 01 PREREQ AUDIT \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 -->\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;margin-top:36px;\">\u00a7 01</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:4px 0 16px 0;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">Prerequisite audit</h2>\n\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr style=\"background:#fafaf7;\"><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">CAPABILITY</th><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">STATUS</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">64+ agents across 6 teams</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#3a6a3a;\">MET</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">7 MCP servers integrated</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#3a6a3a;\">MET</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">28 skills installed</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#3a6a3a;\">MET</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Production hooks</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#a08040;\">PARTIAL (1 hook)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Closed-loop prompts</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#8a3a2a;\">GAP</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Reviewer subagents (Write-restricted)</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#8a3a2a;\">GAP</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Observability / logs</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#8a3a2a;\">GAP</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Orchestrator-capable agents</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#8a3a2a;\">2 of 65</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<div style=\"margin:20px 0; padding:14px 16px; background:#fafaf7; border-left:3px solid #a08040; font-style:italic; color:#666666; font-size:13px;\">\n<strong style=\"color:#a08040;font-style:normal;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">\u2605 BIGGEST FINDING \u2014 </strong>\n63 of 65 agents are leaves \u2014 they cannot autonomously delegate. Most 'multi-agent workflows' were single-agent with future-tense narration ('I'll hand this off to...') that never fired a real Task call.\n</div>\n\n<!-- \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 \u00a7 02 FRAMEWORKS \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 -->\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;margin-top:40px;\">\u00a7 02</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:4px 0 16px 0;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">The three core frameworks</h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:14px;color:#666666;font-style:italic;\">One produces. One refines. One protects.</p>\n\n<!-- Core 4 -->\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:24px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Framework 1 \u2014 The Core Four</h3>\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr><td style=\"width:90px;font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Context</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">What the model can SEE \u2014 files, memory, prior messages</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Model</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Which Claude + reasoning depth (Opus / Sonnet / Haiku)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Prompt</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">The instruction \u2014 slash commands, agent definitions, chat</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Tools</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">What the model can DO \u2014 Read/Write/Bash, MCP, subagents</td></tr>\n</table>\n<div style=\"margin:12px 0; padding:12px 14px; background:#fafaf7; border-left:3px solid #a08040; font-size:12px; color:#666666; font-style:italic;\">\n<strong style=\"color:#a08040;font-style:normal;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DIAGNOSTIC ORDER \u2014 </strong>\nTools first (did agent say can't?) \u2192 Context second (missing info?) \u2192 Prompt third (solved wrong problem?) \u2192 Model last (shallow output?). Most engineers do this in reverse.\n</div>\n\n<!-- 12 Leverage -->\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:24px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Framework 2 \u2014 The 12 Leverage Points (6 Clusters)</h3>\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr><td style=\"width:170px;font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;vertical-align:top;\">A \u00b7 Knowledge Layer</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">CLAUDE.md \u00b7 Agent YAML</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;vertical-align:top;\">B \u00b7 Invocation Layer</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Slash commands \u00b7 Skills</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;vertical-align:top;\">C \u00b7 Delegation Layer</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Subagents (Task tool)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;vertical-align:top;\">D \u00b7 Capability Layer</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">MCP servers \u00b7 Tool permissions</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;vertical-align:top;\">E \u00b7 Enforcement Layer</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Hooks \u00b7 Output routing</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;vertical-align:top;\">F \u00b7 Quality Layer</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Schemas \u00b7 Validators \u00b7 Stdout logs</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#666666;margin:10px 0 0 0;\"><strong>Your cluster strength:</strong> A/B/D strong \u00b7 C/E/F weak. <em>Knowledge-layer-heavy, enforcement-and-quality-layer-light.</em></p>\n\n<!-- 7 Guardrails -->\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:24px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Framework 3 \u2014 The 7 Guardrails <span style=\"color:#a08040;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;\">(your synthesis)</span></h3>\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr><td style=\"width:170px;font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">1. Input validation</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Validate what comes INTO the agent</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">2. Output validation</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Validate what comes OUT before downstream use</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">3. Resource limits</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Cost / time / token caps</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">4. Output routing</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Map output to filesystem location</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">5. Hooks</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Deterministic gates</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">6. Tool permissions</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Allow / deny / ask rules per tool</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">7. Sandbox</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Execution isolation (Docker, restricted FS)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<div style=\"margin:12px 0; padding:12px 14px; background:#fafaf7; border-left:3px solid #a08040; font-size:12px; color:#666666; font-style:italic;\">\n<strong style=\"color:#a08040;font-style:normal;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY THIS FRAMEWORK MATTERS \u2014 </strong>\nDemos prevent embarrassment. Guardrails prevent bankruptcy. Resource limits are the guardrail every demo skips. Yours is the first framework to elevate them as a distinct concept.\n</div>\n\n<!-- \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 \u00a7 03 THE 14 LESSONS \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 -->\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;margin-top:40px;\">\u00a7 03</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:4px 0 16px 0;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">The fourteen lessons</h2>\n\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 01 \u00b7 1H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">The Core Four</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Every AI output = Context + Model + Prompt + Tools. When output is bad, one of these four is the cause.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">80% of engineers reach for the prompt. The real fix is usually Context (wrong files loaded) or Tools (missing capability).</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">Your next debug starts with 'context or tools?' not 'let me rewrite the prompt.'</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 02 \u00b7 1H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">The 12 Leverage Points</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">12 places to inject signal: CLAUDE.md, agent YAML, slash commands, skills, subagents, MCP, hooks, permissions, output routing, schemas, validators, stdout. Group into 6 clusters.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">You use 1-6 and 8-9 actively. Barely use 7 (one hook), 10-12 (no schemas, no validators). Unused points = highest-ROI work.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">Prioritized list of which leverage points to add next.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 03 \u00b7 1.5H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Plan First, Execute Second</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Before asking an agent to DO, ask it to PLAN. Plan goes in a file. You review (5 min). Agent executes against it.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Multi-step work without explicit plans = silent deviations. Plans are exception detectors that catch issues at the cheapest possible time.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">Three of your skills do plan-then-execute instead of execute-blind.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 04 \u00b7 2\u20133H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">PITER / AFK Agents</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Pipeline pattern: Plan \u2192 Implement \u2192 Test \u2192 Evaluate \u2192 Review. Each phase has a gate. You walk away.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Your 17-episode YouTube backlog is the ideal PITER candidate. Each episode follows the same 5-phase shape.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">You run a PITER script for one weekly workflow and walk away for 30 min while it produces a script + storyboard.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 05 \u00b7 2H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Closed Loop Prompts <span style=\"color:#a08040\">\u2605</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Self-correcting loop. Agent runs \u2192 validator checks \u2192 if fail, agent reads the failure and patches \u2192 re-validate \u2192 loop up to N retries \u2192 escalate.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Your PE validation gate is half a closed loop. The other half is auto-fix-and-retry instead of human intervention. Stop being the manual retry button.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">A PE diagnosis can fail validation up to 3 times and still produce a valid PDF without your involvement.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 06 \u00b7 2\u20133H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Specialized Subagents <span style=\"color:#a08040\">\u2605</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">The agent that WRITES should not be the agent that REVIEWS. Three roles: Implementer, Reviewer (Write/Edit excluded), Documenter. The tool restriction IS the separation.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Zero pure reviewer subagents today. Cross-agent review is the highest-leverage QA play you're missing.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">Top-3 most-used pipelines all spawn a reviewer subagent (Write/Edit-restricted) before declaring done.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 07 \u00b7 3H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">ZTE \u2014 Zero Touch Engineering</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Spectrum: in-loop \u2192 out-loop \u2192 ZTE. ZTE = pipeline ships from trigger \u2192 final output with zero human touches. Requires closed loops + reviewers + cron + escalation + audit log.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">lead-gen-cleaning is the cleanest first target. Trigger ready (slash command), sink ready (Sheet), quality bar clear, failure recoverable.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">A lead-gen run happens at 9am Monday without you launching it. Telegram ping at 9:15am. Repeats next Monday. And next.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 08 \u00b7 2H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">The Agentic Layer</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Many agents + hooks + closed loops = distributed system. Distributed systems need infrastructure: structured logs, trace IDs, cost tracking, failure rates, fallback policies.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">You operate 65 agents blind today. Can't answer 'which agent costs me most this week?' That's the operator mindset gap.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">You can answer 'which agent costs me most this week?' in one query against your own JSONL data.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 09 \u00b7 2H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Context Engineering (R+D)</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Retrieve only what's needed + Discard aggressively. Big context costs money, slows down, makes the model dumber. 12 techniques: lazy load, glob over read, ephemeral working files, fresh-context subagents, MCP filtering, memory curation.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Your CLAUDE.md is big. MEMORY.md is bigger. Half is stale. Every prompt loads all of it. Cost AND quality compound negatively.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">MEMORY.md under 4KB with a weekly archiving rhythm.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 10 \u00b7 2H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">The 7 Prompt Levels</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Sophistication ladder: plain \u2192 structured \u2192 few-shot \u2192 templated \u2192 chained \u2192 meta-prompt \u2192 self-improving meta-prompt. Each level abstracts the layer below.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Most of your skills are level 2-3. Slash commands level 4. Nothing is 5+. Meta-prompts (level 6) are where 10\u00d7 productivity lives.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">One production meta-prompt that generates other prompts you actually use.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 11 \u00b7 2H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Domain-Specific Agents</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Specialists outperform generalists on narrow tasks. Encode domain knowledge into the agent. Strict scope, glossary, examples, validation rules, output schema.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Your 6 teams are domain agents at team level. Within teams, agents overlap. MARKETING has 18 agents \u2014 you can't state in one sentence what each one owns.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">Each MARKETING agent has a non-overlapping domain stated in one sentence.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 12 \u00b7 3H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Multi-Agent Orchestration</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">One orchestrator agent receives complex task, decomposes it, dispatches in parallel where possible, aggregates results. Components: orchestrator + specialists + coordination + observability.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">Verified: only 2 of 65 agents have Task in tools. router-agent, cto, cfo-agent, sales-manager, rfp-agent are orchestrators in name only.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">One real workflow runs as \u22653 parallel subagents instead of one sequential agent.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 13 \u00b7 2H</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Skills as Learned Behavior</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Agents forget. Skills are persistent procedures the agent loads when needed. Act-Learn-Reuse: agent acts, captures pattern as skill, reuses next time.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">28 skills, all hand-built. Missing pattern: agent writes its OWN skills from successful runs. Library grows as a side effect of operations.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">Captured \u22652 new skills from real work (not designed in advance) within 30 days.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin:24px 0 28px 0; padding:16px 18px; border-left:3px solid #a08040; background:#fafaf7; font-family:Georgia,serif;\">\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.2em;margin-bottom:4px;\">LESSON 14 \u00b7 4\u20138H + 30D</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#1a1a1a;margin-bottom:10px;\">Capstone \u2014 Codebase Singularity</div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">CONCEPT</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\">Synthesis. Pick one workflow. Apply every lesson (1-13). Run it untouched for 30 days. Prove the system works.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#a08040;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">WHY FOR YOU</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;\">This is Dux Machina's delivery moat. Anyone can sell agentic consulting. Almost nobody can demo a codebase that ships features while the founder sleeps.</span></div>\n  <div style=\"margin:8px 0 0 0;\"><span style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:9px;color:#3a6a3a;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.15em;\">DONE WHEN</span><br>\n    <span style=\"color:#1a1a1a;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:bold;\">Live screen recording of pipeline running with zero human input for 30 days. That becomes the Dux Machina pitch deck slide.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n\n<!-- \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 \u00a7 04 KEY CONCEPTS \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 -->\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;margin-top:40px;\">\u00a7 04</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:4px 0 16px 0;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">Key concepts surfaced beyond the curriculum</h2>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:17px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:20px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Runtime layer \u2014 the kitchen metaphor</h3>\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr style=\"background:#fafaf7;\"><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">COOKS ONLY (CURRENT)</th><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">KITCHEN (RUNTIME LAYER)</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">You invoke each agent manually</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Workflows fire agents through standard channels</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Each call is ad-hoc</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Every call goes through the same plumbing</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">You orchestrate by hand</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">The layer orchestrates itself</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Removing an agent = nothing breaks</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Other parts assume the layer is there</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#666666;margin:10px 0 0 0;font-style:italic;\"><strong>Test:</strong> if you stopped working today, would anything still fire? Today: no. After implementation: yes (cron + ZTE). <em>Presence-without-you is what runtime layer means.</em></p>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:17px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:24px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">The Boring Parts \u2014 your positioning keystone</h3>\n<p style=\"font-size:14px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">\"The boring parts are what people aren't teaching, and if you understand the boring parts, you can handle the output.\"</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:13px;color:#666666;margin:0;\"><strong>Why CFOs care:</strong> Boring = predictable cost. Boring = no 3am pages. Boring = the antidote to AI hype. <em>You sell the boring parts. Everyone else sells the demo.</em></p>\n<p style=\"font-size:13px;color:#666666;margin:10px 0 0 0;\"><strong>Candidate lines for sales:</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"font-size:13px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:6px 0 0 0;padding-left:18px;\">\n<li>\"Most AI consultancies sell you the wallpaper. I install the boring parts that hold the building up.\"</li>\n<li>\"Demos win clicks. Boring parts win contracts.\"</li>\n<li>\"Boring parts compound. Demos depreciate.\"</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:17px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:24px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Where shipping all 14 puts you</h3>\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr style=\"background:#fafaf7;\"><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">CATEGORY</th><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">POPULATION</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">AI consumers</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">~600M</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">AI builders (devs)</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">~5\u201310M</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Multi-agent system builders</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">~50\u2013100K</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Production agentic engineers</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">~1\u20135K</td></tr>\n<tr style=\"background:#fafaf7;\"><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;\">Commercial ZTE operators</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;font-weight:bold;color:#a08040;\">~100\u2013500</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#666666;margin:10px 0 0 0;font-style:italic;\">After shipping all 14 + 60 days operating: top 0.0001% of AI users globally. <strong>Commercial operator</strong> category. <em>Most peers got there from sales side and lack technical depth \u2014 you'd be the engineer in the room.</em></p>\n\n<!-- \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 \u00a7 05 IMPLEMENTATION BACKLOG \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 -->\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;margin-top:40px;\">\u00a7 05</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:4px 0 16px 0;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">Implementation backlog</h2>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:16px 0 6px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Tier 1 \u2014 Structural upgrade (ship first, ~6\u201310h)</h3>\n<ol style=\"font-size:13px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0;padding-left:22px;\">\n<li>PreToolUse hook for output path enforcement</li>\n<li><strong>Upgrade pe_validation_gate.ps1: block + re-invoke up to 3 + escalate on 4th</strong></li>\n<li>Build pe-diagnosis-visual-reviewer subagent (Write/Edit EXCLUDED)</li>\n<li>Build linkedin-brand-reviewer subagent (Write/Edit EXCLUDED)</li>\n<li>JSONL agent run log + 50-line query script</li>\n<li>Curate MEMORY.md \u2192 archive 60% to MEMORY-archive.md</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:16px 0 6px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Tier 2 \u2014 Orchestration (~3h)</h3>\n<ol start=\"7\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0;padding-left:22px;\">\n<li>Promote router-agent, cto, cfo-agent, sales-manager, rfp-agent to real orchestrators (add Task to tools)</li>\n<li>Train orchestrator prompts to batch Task calls for parallelism</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:16px 0 6px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Tier 3 \u2014 Quality + Scale (~6h)</h3>\n<ol start=\"9\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0;padding-left:22px;\">\n<li>Draft schemas/leads.schema.json</li>\n<li>Per-team scope audit (marketing-agent-scope.md)</li>\n<li>First meta-prompt (level 6) \u2014 slash command generator</li>\n<li>capture-as-skill meta-skill</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:16px 0 6px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Tier 4 \u2014 Capstone (4\u20138h build + 30 days run)</h3>\n<ol start=\"13\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0;padding-left:22px;\">\n<li>PE Outreach ZTE pipeline \u2014 combines all of the above</li>\n<li>Run 30 days untouched \u2192 screen recording \u2192 Dux Machina pitch slide</li>\n</ol>\n\n<!-- \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 \u00a7 06 STRATEGIC POSITIONING \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 -->\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;margin-top:40px;\">\u00a7 06</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:24px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:4px 0 16px 0;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">Strategic positioning \u2014 Dux Machina</h2>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:16px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">The one-line offering</h3>\n<p style=\"font-size:14px;color:#1a1a1a;font-style:italic;background:#fafaf7;padding:12px 14px;border-left:3px solid #a08040;margin:0 0 16px 0;\">\n\"Dux Machina installs the boring parts of AI that no one wants to build \u2014 hooks, validators, observability, closed loops \u2014 so your operating costs don't depend on your operations team.\"\n</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:16px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">CFO-language vs CTO-language</h3>\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr style=\"background:#fafaf7;\"><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">CTO LANGUAGE (OTHERS)</th><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">CFO LANGUAGE (YOU)</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Multi-agent orchestration</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Replace contractor hours with capped-cost systems</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">RAG pipelines</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Eliminate $200/hr research overhead</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Agentic workflows</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Boring infrastructure that runs while you sleep</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Latest LLM capabilities</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">30-day demo of zero-touch operation</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Cutting-edge AI</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Predictable monthly spend with hard caps</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:16px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:20px 0 8px 0;font-weight:normal;\">Pricing tiers (post-capstone)</h3>\n<table cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr style=\"background:#fafaf7;\"><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">TIER</th><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">DELIVERABLE</th><th align=\"left\" style=\"color:#a08040;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.15em;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;\">PRICE</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Diagnosis</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">1-page PE-style firm diagnosis</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">$0\u2013500</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Discovery + plan</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Audit + 14-leverage scan + ZTE roadmap</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">$5K\u201315K</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">First pipeline install</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">One ZTE pipeline + 30 days operation + handoff</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">$25K\u201350K</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Quarterly retainer</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Ongoing operations + new pipelines</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">$10K\u201325K/mo</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Fractional CTO</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Strategic + tactical agentic ownership</td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">$15K\u201335K/mo</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 CLOSING \u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550 -->\n<hr style=\"border:none;border-top:1px solid #cccccc;margin:36px 0 20px 0;\">\n\n<div style=\"background:#fafaf7;padding:20px 22px;border-left:3px solid #a08040;margin:24px 0;\">\n<div style=\"font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#a08040;letter-spacing:0.3em;font-weight:bold;\">SINGLE NEXT ACTION</div>\n<p style=\"font-size:15px;color:#1a1a1a;margin:8px 0 0 0;line-height:1.55;\">\nOpen <code style=\"background:#fff;padding:1px 5px;border:1px solid #cccccc;font-size:13px;\">LEARNING/sweep-complete.md</code>. Ship Tier 1 item #2 \u2014 upgrade <code style=\"background:#fff;padding:1px 5px;border:1px solid #cccccc;font-size:13px;\">pe_validation_gate.ps1</code> from \"block + page\" to \"block + re-invoke + escalate.\" <strong>~30 minutes of focused work.</strong> After that, you have one production closed loop and Lesson 5 is genuinely Done.\n</p>\n</div>\n\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#666666;font-style:italic;margin:24px 0 0 0;\">Compiled 2026-05-11 \u00b7 Dux Machina \u00b7 Field Manual N\u00b0 01 \u00b7 Reverse-engineered + personalized</p>\n\n</div><